From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:04:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Icon-tag report headings and dropdown stat counts; drop boxed
 Clean pill
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SimpleMarkdown: headings matching known operational sections (severity,
data gaps, next-steps, recommended actions) get a small icon prefix so
they read as signals to act on instead of blending into the surrounding
prose — keyword-matched against the LLM's own heading text since its
exact wording varies per run; anything else renders unchanged.

Leak Map audit picker: the "Clean" status pill had a one-off
bg/border override that put it back in the boxed-pill shape
status-pill.tsx explicitly moved away from everywhere else — now uses
the same plain-colored-text "success" tone as every other status.
The issue/alert counts on each row get small icons too, so they don't
read as a bare number wall.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkznvRLnBokzbdmJ2WwaEM
